on is payable on a shortfall. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check is nowhere near tripping (no_show_terminations_30d 0 against completed_trips_30d 54), and no limb of POL-NS-09 escalation is met, so this is a money case and not a hold.\n\nTO THE RIDER. Your claim under POL-NS-06 is accepted: the measured dwell is 144 seconds against a required 180, a 36-second shortfall, and that alone refunds the fee. Your POL-NS-04 exoneration claim is rejected, and you do not need it: limb (b) fails because the driver replied 'ok' at 13:33:11, within 120 seconds of your 13:32:56 message, and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty, so the unanswered-contact route is closed. Your point that the driver's 'not visible' account is contradicted by his own record is noted — your track places you within about 19 m of the pin throughout, and you said you were in the lobby and coming out — but POL-NS-06 refunds the fee regardless of presence, so nothing turns on it. The driver's contrary limb (a), (b) and (d) claims are accepted only so far as they go: (a) and (b) hold, (d) does not.\n\nTHE MONEY. EV-FARE-02707 shows a single cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.50, total charged SGD 4.50, base fare and waiting-time line zero, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. The whole contested SGD 4.50 is refunded, and nothing else on this trip is in issue (the gross SGD 6.61 is not a sum charged here). No driver compensation is payable. Every artifact this ruling rests on is admissible at weight 1.0, except the MISSING advisory, which carries no fact in this case; the confidence cap is therefore 1.0 and the ruling is issued at 0.95. The monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically, subject to the appeal route, which this notice carries."
